#13's fix is committed and queued to land, but it isn't verified: the build service returned no result in 3 hours. So nothing has merged, `v0.1.3` isn't tagged and the issue stays open.

**The fix** (`42b42cf` on `looper/opa-13`):
- `parseTokenUse` now handles the numbers OPA returns (`json.Number`), plus Go's `float64`, `int64` and `int`. A number is accepted only if it is a whole number that maps to a real TokenUse value, so nothing gets truncated. This also covers #12. The string forms (`"TOKEN_USE_EXTERNAL"`, `"EXTERNAL"`) still work.
- As Jody's triage asked, any other `token_use` (`4294967302`, `6.5`, `9999`, an unknown name, `null`, …) now makes `EvalProxyPolicy` fail with `codes.Internal`. Before, it silently became TOKEN_USE_UNSPECIFIED. Leaving `token_use` out still means unspecified.
- The tests in `internal/handler_proxy_token_use_test.go` run real policies through `EvalProxyPolicy`.
- I committed a PROPOSALS.md follow-up separately (`6704cb2`). The proxy policy's other result fields still drop a value of the wrong type silently.

**Not verified:**
- Build pipeline 3059162868 ended with "no verdict within 3h". That means the build never reported back, not that a gate failed.
- No opa build has returned a verdict since 2026-11-11; #11, #12 and #14 ended the same way. This is the known outage in tacplus-dev/looper#113, #128 and tacplus-dev/cluster#18.
- I couldn't compile or run the tests here: there's no container runtime and the generated code is absent. Only `gofmt` was checked, and it's clean.
- `looper-trace check` passes. `EvalProxyPolicy` makes no outgoing calls, so there is no `trace_id` to pass on.

**What happens next:**
- The land has been queued since 11:56Z. If the gates pass, the manager merges it after this run ends.
- The next run then runs `just gates` on main, tags and pushes `v0.1.3`, comments and closes #13. There's no release/0.1 branch, so nothing needs backporting.
- #12's queued branch calls `parseTokenUse` the old way, so whichever of #12 and #13 lands second has to be updated to match.

I posted this status on #13 and wrote `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#113` and `Blocked-by: tacplus-dev/looper#128` to the outcome file, so the issue is worked again once both close.
